# unit-watch-ends-off.vrs: unit-watch D27 part 2, the watch off. Run after unit-watch-ends.vrs and a restart with
# [UnitWatch] Enabled = false in the dev cfg (set it back to true after this run). uw-wave runs at uw-a with Chaos there
# (A3: no sunk spider, a sunk unit does not stay sunk; with the watch off nothing would mark one anyway): no "[nyar] unit-watch" line in 2 x StuckSeconds (180 s at the default
# 90), `event info` shows "unit watch: off", and `.nyar event unstick uw-wave` replies "unit watch is off: [UnitWatch]
# Enabled" and changes nothing. The previous boot's uw-wave instance was cancelled by the restart: no unit-watch line for it
# is read from this boot's log (checked by hand from the log copy, as the run starts after the boot).
#
# Needs: what unit-watch-ends.vrs needs, with Enabled = false; the mark uw-a (made by unit-watch-ends.vrs).
ensure
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
console TPHome
wait 3
chat .devgo uw-a
expect-log \[DEV TP\] uw-a
wait 4
console ToggleInvulnerable true
wait 2
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
mark
chat .nyar event start uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave wave 1/2 timeout=30
wait 8
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch timeout=180
chat .nyar event info uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch: off
chat .nyar event unstick uw-wave
expect-reply unit watch is off: [UnitWatch] Enabled
wait 2
shot chat uw-unstick-off
expect-no-log \[nyar\] unit-watch timeout=15
chat .nyar event stop uw-wave
expect-log event uw-wave stopped
chat .nyar status
expect-reply tracked units: 0 timeout=40
console TPHome
wait 3
